From 9b387e2dcc71bcf295ed935efb84b01224f4c9a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xenia UI <ui@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:47:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] [App] Add the game library window and wire it into the
 main window

LibraryDialog is a launcher shown while no title is running:

* Game folders (added from the sidebar, recursive or not) are scanned in the
  background; the sidebar filters by All / Favorites / Recently played / a
  single folder, with a context menu per folder.
* Grid or list view, search (name, title id, file name; Ctrl+F), five sort
  orders, adjustable card size, all remembered in the config.
* A details panel with Play, favorite, rename and per-game settings, and a
  context menu on every game. Double-click, Enter or the gamepad A button
  plays; Y toggles favorite.
* Icons are shown once a game has been run (they are cached from the running
  title); other games get a coloured placeholder.

EmulatorWindow owns the library and its icon cache, adds File > Game Library
and File > Settings..., records every successful launch (from any path:
Open, drag and drop, recents, command line, library) and brings the library
back if a launch fails, before the error message so the message stays on top.
Opening a file from the library goes through a deferred call because
RunTitle() tears down all dialogs, including the one that called it.
